From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shcore: explicit AppUserModelID, scale factors, scale change registrations, IsOS

- SetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID kept nothing and
  GetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID failed with E_NOTIMPL (taskbar
  grouping, jump lists and toasts key on the ID). The ID (at most 128
  characters) is kept; Get gives a copy, E_FAIL when none was set.
- GetScaleFactorForMonitor and GetScaleFactorForDevice said 100% whatever
  the DPI; they give the scale factor nearest the monitor's effective DPI
  (144 dpi is 150%).
- RegisterScaleChangeEvent and RegisterScaleChangeNotifications failed
  with E_NOTIMPL: a hidden window hears the display and settings
  broadcasts and, when the primary display's scale factor changes, sets
  the registered events and posts the registered windows their message.
  UnregisterScaleChangeEvent and RevokeScaleChangeNotifications are
  exported.
- SHReleaseThreadRef did nothing: it releases the thread's reference.
- IsOS answered OS_TERMINALCLIENT, OS_TABLETPC, OS_MEDIACENTER,
  OS_FASTUSERSWITCHING, OS_WELCOMELOGONUI, OS_EMBEDDED, OS_APPLIANCE and
  OS_SERVERADMINUI with FIXMEs (and some wrongly: the sign-in screen is a
  welcome screen). OS_DOMAINMEMBER, which says yes for every machine, is
  left as it is.
- Feature state queries and subscriptions stop logging FIXMEs: no feature
  is ever overridden here.

Wine's shcore tests: no failures, as before.

Gate: test/shcorebits-gate.sh (Xvfb, 144 dpi). Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_AUMID,
SG_MUTANT_NO_SCALE_FACTOR (shcore/main.c).
